                <pb facs="0806" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">600.127/264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Charge at Mexico City</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ferris</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-23T11:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 23,
                                1922—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:12
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Decree published and effective February 21st provides that export duties on
                    petroleum and its derivatives established June 7th, 1921 may be paid Mexican
                    gold or bonds of the public debt as may be determined.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ferris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
